                <syl /><neume facs="#m-f61f974f-279a-4d66-bbfb-6251d01ad821" type="punctum" xml:id="m-7b948991-5f86-4e6b-9643-37e52bdb2c0d">
                  <nc xml:id="m-015016c4-eaf4-4b20-a5f9-e5c38be523d0" pname="a" oct="3">
                    <signifLet xml:id="m-8fba70d9-e330-4a4a-83e7-7c31a1bcfcc5" /></nc></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-14df04ef-5858-48e8-83bc-077b5af05428">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-c7b1b14d-f2b2-45c8-99da-9a67044f97d9" type="punctum" xml:id="m-e67178c1-06dd-4b88-831e-0244c59ec562">
                  <nc xml:id="m-7af4b7ba-24c9-4ed0-9fa5-d10fdc1d63f3" pname="c" oct="4" /></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-f6e565b8-867d-4c91-9ced-46f690be94de">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-c9fa2684-3002-4b41-a1b3-89e2a5e5759d" type="punctum" xml:id="m-c0116ea3-2f0d-4208-99ae-fc69699e3641">
                  <nc xml:id="m-b13b85d9-7fc6-442c-9b0e-6afedb147dc2" pname="c" oct="4" /></neume></syllable><syllable xml:id="m-f6dae3d4-9219-4ae1-99a3-6953c8623825">
                <syl /><neume facs="#m-58b6ebee-3b55-451d-9d54-300de93bb065" type="punctum" xml:id="m-bedf5188-035f-45d2-ab1d-780de3c3e0a7">
                  <nc xml:id="m-b204fc43-f8e0-4a1b-adfb-f5e9ff876a8c" pname="c" oct="4" /></neume></syllable><divLine xml:id="m-0013b201-0868-468f-b3d3-8ab9e110cb28" facs="#m-d52db6c7-ab25-432e-8c89-efca14b0e4c5" form="finalis" /></layer></staff><div xml:id="m-004d732d-27a8-41d9-8b2e-5f82d4c9d084"><lg xml:id="m-788eb853-ea48-4d0b-8fea-68380d219980"><l xml:id="m-43807e29-21c2-4b78-a312-f9ba42668836" facs="#m-20c7d048-6995-4a88-be22-e738714c63b4" label="text-like">THE OFFICE FOR THE DEAD</l><l xml:id="m-df39489a-ff7c-4b57-ad27-476da248ec1d" facs="#m-bf114edf-1bdc-42b3-bb32-53b42afa4191" label="text-like">At the Office for the Dead, the Antiphons are doubled whenever the Office</l><l xml:id="m-bd7453fe-b8a2-45cd-addb-7dbeaaecc47f" facs="#m-585238db-2613-40b7-b4ea-c67974b3a164" label="text-like">is celebrated solemnly. They are also doubled on the dar of the burial. on</l><l xml:id="m-10bf1dd6-40cd-4c2b-a6da-cfb277101bad" facs="#m-ae5e5b52-7f04-431e-9837-39423b499dc9" label="lyrics-like">the day folloming thẽ announcement of the death, on the ihird, seventh, and</l><l xml:id="m-7a348543-1e51-4301-a698-65ae8209d85d" facs="#m-2438cdd8-6fcd-4cb7-9871-a2ccc9bc7663" label="text-like">thirtieth days after the death, and on the anniversary dars seven on such</l><l xml:id="m-1db56d01-9f2b-4d50-8772-52099eb4178d" facs="#m-531b7da3-bc1c-4036-bdc9-3a701590a45d" label="text-like">general anniversaries as, for instance, the Anniversary of all the deceased or</l><l xml:id="m-9b1ba3a5-2adf-442d-8d58-0ede4689c940" facs="#m-b9fc8043-1de2-4184-96ab-b874e382e574" label="text-like">a religions order or the Anniversary of those who fell in war.) </l><l xml:id="m-c48fd454-2708-4ca7-ba22-65a3b40cac3e" facs="#m-75de244e-2b0e-49ff-8a42-66f790c8c364" label="lyrics-like">of each psalm, the V. Réquiem aetérnam* dóna eis Dómine. Et lux perpétua</l><l xml:id="m-439bcc55-6d93-4dd3-b861-a3bea3334a79" facs="#m-0e916fa7-0148-4fb4-8b70-a65fcb946cc1" label="lyrics-like">lúceat éis is always said, even if the Ofice be for one person onty. The first</l><l xml:id="m-3040e3ed-e4aa-443e-826a-8dfd49d78218" facs="#m-2bd8610e-42a0-43e0-a805-d16a2febc10c" label="text-like">verse of each psalm is always intoned as indicated, even when the Antiphons</l><l xml:id="m-41feccb1-61dd-4dac-9e5f-6e00caf1cd9f" facs="#m-46d43fcf-822e-429c-b5d1-17922f426d1c" label="text-like">are not doubled.</l><l xml:id="m-f4273e0a-2c98-48cd-8243-fc3d415ead64" facs="#m-0d413aec-71c1-4489-aaaf-ea040c003f05" label="text-like">AT VESPERS.</l><l xml:id="m-df103130-9a56-4d9e-8d65-8d8a8dd402cd" facs="#m-4254e94d-96b5-405c-b909-f1a7568a6b7a" label="text-like">If Vespers are said on the day or the burial, the Office begins directlx</l><l xml:id="m-734b2516-8f6a-45af-94b8-f5e2c0da89ff" facs="#m-fd4af74e-2872-4063-9942-fb1c8b3e5680" label="text-like">bythe first Antiphon, after the Responsory Subvenite, or after the</l><l xml:id="m-13541386-8e4a-4cab-b48d-a1c5311d415f" facs="#m-3a42e11f-4b4c-4b5d-93dd-bd18eb2e688c" label="text-like">Vespers of the day. On all other occasions, Pater and Ave are first said</l><l xml:id="m-9dca65b4-aeaa-4317-9c82-cafef04eb0d0" facs="#m-cb32b64e-c8aa-4c18-a8a2-baff5aed9b3c" label="ambiguous">silentiy.</l><l xml:id="m-93c5030e-7d70-4615-9c2c-dbba155e94c7" facs="#m-0298fbdb-37c3-4dc7-b3a3-b6c7aa199cab" label="ambiguous">1.Ant.E</l><l xml:id="m-09e70f7d-0e47-4f8c-bb86-80ff5b29384f" facs="#m-ae70b475-697e-47d0-8978-01e209dfb693" label="ambiguous">3.b</l><l xml:id="m-5972acea-c76c-49b5-a8bd-9c94f78ca7a6" facs="#m-cd9bc319-43ec-407a-92c9-69bf4e537e39" label="lyrics-like">Lacébo Dómino" in regi-6̂-ne vi-vó-rum.</l><l xml:id="m-ad1ca156-93b2-4fae-81e7-f900b3ecf536" facs="#m-59daa7af-ffa0-49a5-a28c-ebf650404471" label="ambiguous">Psalm 114.</l><l xml:id="m-2f881c62-2044-4510-b151-373e094e5c01" facs="#m-b54a970c-49fe-4d96-aa46-4e9d8172c8c1" label="lyrics-like">1. Di-léxi, quóni-am exáudi-et Dómi-nus “vócem ora¬</l><l xml:id="m-fcb2cfc5-d657-4591-91b1-c509c760c810" facs="#m-284e4bca-5af4-41f6-8e35-7b0ba41d161a" label="lyrics-like">ti-ónis mé¬ ae. Flex: mé-am:</l><l xml:id="m-be302443-2908-4865-b80a-adc9784679dc" facs="#m-2bc86688-a7f8-4991-b0b4-77961b4e1fb2" label="lyrics-like">2. Quia inclinávit áurem súam mihi:“t in diébus méis invocábo.</l><l xml:id="m-e0839499-39a3-4fd4-9395-a3cce7decc8d" facs="#m-ede611f8-2d06-4780-a861-3041b421974c" label="lyrics-like">3. Circumdedérunt me dolóres mórtiset pericula inférni</l><l xml:id="m-fca5a934-3c85-465d-958d-ca24e7382b6d" facs="#m-b8121af7-826b-4cd6-bd5a-b5a580f37169" label="lyrics-like">invenérunt me.</l><l xml:id="m-8fd35dcb-6a99-4061-b073-efd4b60c2fc1" facs="#m-b05577db-e350-49e6-b859-de28a1a31e3d" label="lyrics-like">4. Tribulatiónem et dolórem invéni:“ et nómen Dómini invoeávi.</l><l xml:id="m-8b09d41c-1aac-421d-81cb-ea6cd934c43f" facs="#m-c7dae838-741a-46b4-9c66-6dea446096f6" label="lyrics-like">5. O Dómine libera ánimam méam:t miséricors Dóminus, et</l><l xml:id="m-7389edf6-7303-4ea2-98f4-5cfe2d3111f0" facs="#m-f0cd6315-fd36-4839-8998-93215ed6bfc8" label="lyrics-like">jústus,*et Déus nóster miserétur.</l><l xml:id="m-537c37f0-b62e-4c4d-9afe-651a0ff5a10b" facs="#m-b2711576-061f-4f77-be6d-30c356c35eec" label="lyrics-like">6. Custódiens párvulos Dóminus:“ humiliátus sum, et liberávit me¬</l><l xml:id="m-d5df5c5a-b2fe-4664-af31-58150a5e44cb" facs="#m-ce5efac0-c9de-455d-abfe-b9aebcae8149" label="lyrics-like">7. Convértere ánima méa in réquiem túam:“qua Dóminus bene¬</l><l xml:id="m-8bd0f202-b847-4fc1-9e20-e4d7b771ff32" facs="#m-ef27b29e-b8f0-4c2b-aef4-93875ccb7a45" label="lyrics-like">fécit tibi.</l><l xml:id="m-3d932e68-fd4e-441f-ad0e-05da00e999cc" facs="#m-737ebbee-5603-4ee9-b8c4-08af520b7387" label="lyrics-like">8. Quia erípuit ánimam méam de mórte: t óculos méos a láerimis,</l><l xml:id="m-1869e597-eca1-4579-808c-fd10f9af65f4" facs="#m-c1de9248-bdb6-432b-9f97-3fa031237bb9" label="lyrics-like">pédes méos a lápsu.</l><l xml:id="m-66b152f3-11ef-4fdf-b945-bc7763eab739" facs="#m-65477050-3a41-4e2a-b22e-2466de490397" label="lyrics-like">9. Placébo Dómino“ in regióne vivórum.</l><l xml:id="m-6612fedc-1942-4fc3-840a-1d912bb304ef" facs="#m-01da2028-8d7e-4f1c-80fa-661664a50199" label="lyrics-like">10. Réquiem aetérnam* dóna éis Dómine.</l><l xml:id="m-a3de8fe8-1f2f-4f5c-b934-d39dd220b012" facs="#m-c7c73dff-d31a-4969-accc-ffc432fc623d" label="lyrics-like">11. Et lux perpétua * lúceat éis.</l><l xml:id="m-84ca964d-1627-490e-a66d-2dcddcfe1ce8" facs="#m-8dcb0b16-80bb-4816-8ff5-63e9e83738c2" label="text-like">The Antiphon is reveated after each Psalm.</l></lg></div></section></score></mdiv></body></music>
</mei>